            <div class="seo-block">
                <h2>Comprehensive Guide: How to Convert BMP to PNG</h2>
                <p>Converting your files from <strong>BMP</strong> to <strong>PNG</strong> is a great way to manage compatibility, visual quality, and storage weight. This tool lets you perform this entire conversion locally in your browser, keeping your data 100% private.</p>
                <p><strong>What is BMP?</strong> BMP (Bitmap) is a classic raster graphics image file format developed by Microsoft. It stores image pixels without compression (or with minimal compression), preserving perfect quality but resulting in extremely large file sizes.</p>
                <p><strong>What is PNG?</strong> PNG (Portable Network Graphics) is a raster-based image format that supports lossless data compression. It was designed to replace GIF and is widely used across the web for images requiring transparency or crisp detail like logos and text.</p>
                <p><strong>Why convert BMP to PNG?</strong> The primary reason to perform this conversion is optimization. If you need to make your website load faster, shifting heavy images to lighter formats like WebP or JPG is key. On the other hand, if you need transparency or need to edit designs, converting to PNG is ideal. Because our application is 100% local, your original files are processed on your RAM and never leave your computer, ensuring absolute privacy and saving you internet bandwidth.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="seo-block" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3>How to Convert BMP to PNG in 3 Simple Steps</h3>
