        <section class="seo-content-section">
            <div class="seo-block">
                <h2>Comprehensive Guide: How to Convert JPG to PDF</h2>
                <p>Converting your files from <strong>JPG</strong> to <strong>PDF</strong> is a great way to manage compatibility, visual quality, and storage weight. This tool lets you perform this entire conversion locally in your browser, keeping your data 100% private.</p>
                <p><strong>What is JPG?</strong> JPG/JPEG (Joint Photographic Experts Group) is the most popular image format in the world. It uses lossy compression to dramatically reduce file sizes, making it perfect for photographs and web loading, though it does not support transparent backgrounds.</p>
                <p><strong>What is PDF?</strong> PDF (Portable Document Format) is a global standard developed by Adobe for presenting and sharing documents reliably, independent of the software, hardware, or operating system being used.</p>
                <p><strong>Why convert JPG to PDF?</strong> The primary reason to perform this conversion is optimization. If you need to make your website load faster, shifting heavy images to lighter formats like WebP or JPG is key. On the other hand, if you need transparency or need to edit designs, converting to PNG is ideal. Because our application is 100% local, your original files are processed on your RAM and never leave your computer, ensuring absolute privacy and saving you internet bandwidth.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="seo-block" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3>How to Convert JPG to PDF in 3 Simple Steps</h3>
                <ol class="seo-steps-list">
                    <li><strong>1. Upload your JPG files:</strong> Drag and drop your files into the upload box above, or click the box to browse your device files.</li>
                    <li><strong>2. Instant Conversion:</strong> The tool automatically reads the files. Click "Convert" to transform them using your web browser's native API.</li>
                    <li><strong>3. Download PDF:</strong> Click download on each file card, or download everything as a single ZIP file. It is that simple, secure, and fast!</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

            <section class="faq-section" style="margin-top: 3rem;">
                <div class="faq-header">
                    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) about JPG to PDF</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-list">
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3>Is my data secure when converting JPG to PDF?</h3>
                        <p>Yes, completely. All conversion calculations are done locally in your browser using HTML5 Canvas and File Reader APIs. Your files are never uploaded to any server, so your photos remain private.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3>Can I convert multiple JPG files at once?</h3>
                        <p>Absolutely! Our converter supports batch processing. You can load up to 5 files simultaneously for free, or upgrade to our PRO plan for unlimited bulk uploads.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h3>Will I lose quality after converting to PDF?</h3>
                        <p>Converting to lossy formats like JPG may introduce slight compression differences, but our tool uses maximum canvas rendering settings to ensure your output looks crisp and clean.</p>
