                <div class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>What is WebP?</h2>
                    <p>WebP is a modern image format developed by Google that provides superior lossless and lossy compression for web images, helping to load pages faster and consume less bandwidth.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>When to use JPG</h2>
                    <p>JPG is best for standard photographic content where universal compatibility across legacy clients and photo printing services is required.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="privacy-card">
                    <h2>When to use PNG</h2>
                    <p>PNG is the standard for illustrations, logos, vector icons, screenshots containing text, or any graphics that require transparent background elements.</p>
                </div>
