        <section class="seo-content-section">
            <div class="seo-block">
                <h2>Comprehensive Guide: How to Convert HEIC to JPG</h2>
                <p>Converting your files from <strong>HEIC</strong> to <strong>JPG</strong> is a great way to manage compatibility, visual quality, and storage weight. This tool lets you perform this entire conversion locally in your browser, keeping your data 100% private.</p>
                <p><strong>What is HEIC?</strong> HEIC (High Efficiency Image Container) is Apple's default image format for iPhones and iPads. It offers excellent visual quality at half the file size of a traditional JPG, but lacks native compatibility on non-Apple operating systems.</p>
                <p><strong>What is JPG?</strong> JPG/JPEG (Joint Photographic Experts Group) is the most popular image format in the world. It uses lossy compression to dramatically reduce file sizes, making it perfect for photographs and web loading, though it does not support transparent backgrounds.</p>
                <p><strong>Why convert HEIC to JPG?</strong> The primary reason to perform this conversion is optimization. If you need to make your website load faster, shifting heavy images to lighter formats like WebP or JPG is key. On the other hand, if you need transparency or need to edit designs, converting to PNG is ideal. Because our application is 100% local, your original files are processed on your RAM and never leave your computer, ensuring absolute privacy and saving you internet bandwidth.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="seo-block" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3>How to Convert HEIC to JPG in 3 Simple Steps</h3>
                <ol class="seo-steps-list">
                    <li><strong>1. Upload your HEIC files:</strong> Drag and drop your files into the upload box above, or click the box to browse your device files.</li>
